## Key Decision Points

### Tech Stack

- **Framework**: SvelteKit (not Next.js or plain React)
- **UI Library**: shadcn-svelte (Svelte port of shadcn/ui - copy-paste components)
- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS 4.1.17 (full customization via component files)
- **Host**: Cloudflare Workers (not traditional Node server)
- **Database**: D1 SQLite (not PostgreSQL) - Phase 2
- **Storage**: R2 object storage (not GCS or S3) - Phase 2
- **Auth**: Cloudflare Zero Trust (MVP) + optional SvelteKit auth (Phase 3)
- **Why**: Edge computing + integrated ecosystem + learning goal + familiar component patterns

### Architecture

- **Components**: Live in `/src/routes` and `/src/lib/components`
- **Business Logic**: Lives in `/src/lib/services`
- **Types**: Centralized in `/src/lib/types`
- **Stores**: Svelte stores in `/src/lib/stores` for state
- **No**: Business logic in components; complex components in routes

### UI Inspiration & Implementation

- **Google Drive**-like interface - familiar UX for users
- shadcn-svelte components provide the building blocks
- Sidebar navigation + main content area
- Grid/list view toggle
- Drag & drop folder management
- Tag-based search/filtering
- **Key Components**: Button, Card, Dialog, Input, Tabs, Breadcrumb, DropdownMenu, ContextMenu

### Phase 1: UI-First Development Strategy

**Goal**: Build fully interactive Google Drive-like interface with mocked data (no backend yet)

- **Mock Data**: Lives in `src/lib/data/mock.ts`, seeded by `PUBLIC_USE_MOCK_DATA` env var
- **State**: Svelte stores in `src/lib/stores/` (workspace, folders, files, tags, selection)
- **Demo Page**: `/demo` showcases mocked CMS (public example)
- **Production**: When `PUBLIC_USE_MOCK_DATA` unset, queries go to real D1 backend (Phase 2)
- **UI Testing**: Local browser testing with no API calls needed
- **Easy Migration**: Once Phase 2 starts, swap mock data queries with real D1 queries

### Phase 2: Cloudflare Backend

- Connect D1 database queries
- R2 file upload integration
- Search with D1 queries
- Sessions with D1 storage

## Styling Guidelines

### ✅ DO: Use Theme Colors

**Always use shadcn theme colors from `src/routes/layout.css`**

Available theme CSS variables:

- `primary` / `primary-foreground` - Primary actions
- `secondary` / `secondary-foreground` - Secondary actions
- `accent` / `accent-foreground` - Orange highlights (buttons, CTAs)
- `muted` / `muted-foreground` - Disabled/inactive states
- `background` / `foreground` - Page background and text
- `card` - Card backgrounds
- `border` - Border color
- `destructive` - Error/delete actions
- `sidebar-*` - Sidebar variants

**Examples:**

```svelte
<!-- ✅ CORRECT -->
<button class="bg-accent text-accent-foreground">Action</button>
<div class="border-b border-border">Content</div>
<p class="text-muted-foreground">Disabled</p>
```

### ❌ DON'T: Use Raw Tailwind Colors

Never hardcode color classes. They break theming:

```svelte
<!-- ❌ WRONG - Never do this -->
<button class="bg-blue-500 text-white">Bad</button>
<div class="border-red-200">Wrong</div>
<p class="text-gray-600">Bad</p>
```

### ✅ DO: Use Lucide Icons

**Import ONLY from `@lucide/svelte`**:

```typescript
import { Plus, Trash2, Edit, Folder, File, Grid3x3, List, Search, Upload, ChevronDown, MoreVertical } from '@lucide/svelte';
```

Common icon categories:

- **Navigation**: Folder, File, Grid3x3, List, ChevronDown, ChevronUp, ChevronRight
- **Actions**: Plus, Edit, Trash2, Upload, Download, Copy, Share2
- **UI**: Search, MoreVertical, MoreHorizontal, X, Check, AlertCircle, Clock
- **Status**: CheckCircle, AlertCircle, InfoCircle, XCircle

**Usage:**

```svelte
<script>
	import { Plus } from '@lucide/svelte';
</script>

<!-- ✅ CORRECT -->
<Plus class="h-4 w-4" />

<!-- ❌ NEVER -->
<span>➕</span>
```

### ❌ DON'T: Use Emojis

Never use emojis in code:

```svelte
<!-- ❌ WRONG - Never do this -->
<div>📁 My Folder</div>
<button>⬆️ Upload</button>
<span>❌ Delete</span>
```

## File Structure Reference

```
/
├── README.md                 ← Project overview
├── PROJECT_CONTEXT.md        ← Architecture & decisions (READ FIRST)
├── ROADMAP.md                ← Phase breakdown & timeline
